    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2019-june/q7",
      "question": "<p>In a simple model, the value, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds V\"></span>, of a car depends on its age, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>, in years.</p><p>The following information is available for car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span></p><ul><li>its value when new is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds 20\\,000\"></span></li><li>its value after one year is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds 16\\,000\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Use an exponential model to form, for car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, a possible equation linking <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The value of car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is monitored over a 10-year period.<br>Its value after 10 years is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds 2\\,000\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Evaluate the reliability of your model in light of this information. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The following information is available for car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span></p><ul><li>it has the same value, when new, as car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span></li><li>its value depreciates more slowly than that of car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Explain how you would adapt the equation found in (a) so that it could be used to model the value of car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
