    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2019-june/q8",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:70mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2019-june/q08-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2: sketch of the cubic y = x(x + 2)(x - 4) through O; R1 is shaded between the curve and the negative x-axis; R2 is shaded below the positive x-axis between the curve and the line x = b.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of part of the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x(x+2)(x-4)\"></span>.</p><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R_1\"></span> shown shaded in Figure 2 is bounded by the curve and the negative <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that the exact area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R_1\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{20}{3}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R_2\"></span> also shown shaded in Figure 2 is bounded by the curve, the positive <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis and the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=b\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> is a positive constant and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;b&lt;4\"></span></p><p>Given that the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R_1\"></span> is equal to the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R_2\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>verify that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> satisfies the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(b+2)^2\\left(3b^2-20b+20\\right)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The roots of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3b^2-20b+20=0\"></span> are 1.225 and 5.442 to 3 decimal places.<br>The value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> is therefore 1.225 to 3 decimal places.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Explain, with the aid of a diagram, the significance of the root 5.442 <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
