    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2019-june/q10",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Prove that for all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^2+2\"></span> is not divisible by 4 <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>“Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\in\\mathbb R\"></span>, the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left|3x-28\\right|\"></span> is greater than or equal to the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x-9)\"></span>.”<br>State, giving a reason, if the above statement is always true, sometimes true or never true. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
