      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2019-june/q11",
      "question": "<p>A competitor is running a 20 kilometre race.</p><p>She runs each of the first 4 kilometres at a steady pace of 6 minutes per kilometre.<br>After the first 4 kilometres, she begins to slow down.</p><p>In order to estimate her finishing time, the time that she will take to complete each subsequent kilometre is modelled to be 5% greater than the time that she took to complete the previous kilometre.</p><p>Using the model,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that her time to run the first 6 kilometres is estimated to be 36 minutes 55 seconds, <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>show that her estimated time, in minutes, to run the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span>th kilometre, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\leqslant r\\leqslant 20\"></span>, is<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"6\\times 1.05^{r-4}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>estimate the total time, in minutes and seconds, that she will take to complete the race. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
