    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2019-june/q13",
      "question": "<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{p-3x}{(2x-q)(x+3)}\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R,\\ x\\neq -3,\\ x\\neq 2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are constants, passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(3,\\dfrac12\\right)\"></span> and has two vertical asymptotes with equations <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-3\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Explain why you can deduce that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=4\"></span></li><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=15\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol></li></ol><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:65mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2019-june/q13-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 4: sketch of part of the curve C for x &gt; 0, decreasing and crossing the x-axis; the region R between C, the x-axis and the line x = 3 is shaded.\"></figure><p>Figure 4 shows a sketch of part of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>. The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 4, is bounded by the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis and the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Show that the exact value of the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\ln 2+b\\ln 3\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are rational constants to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(8)</span></li></ol>",
